+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling One Stays Out
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined "changing or cancelling a visit once booked". The [2026-08-08 non-goal ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) confirmed it deliberate and treated a booked visit as immutable. That ADR also set the rule for reopening the row: only an explicit owner decision recorded at intake narrows it, never the request alone.
+
+A request on 2026-09-11 asks for correcting a booked visit. It comes with the owner's decision on NG-5, quoted verbatim from the intake record:
+
+> "Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in. Record the narrowing the way the project records non-goal changes."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** Rejected by the owner's decision above.
+2. **Drop NG-5 entirely.** Rejected: the owner keeps cancellation out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation** (chosen, per the owner's decision).
+
+## Decision
+
+A booked visit's date and description can be corrected; [REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) states the capability. Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, and NG-5 now declines only that.
+
+The owner also decided how this first step reaches staff: "The edit form is reachable by its URL alone: the owner detail page gains no edit link in this request. A visible entry point may come as a follow-up request." That is deferred, not declined, so it adds no Non-Goals row.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample now corrects visits forward, as it already does owner and pet details. It still deletes nothing (NG-4) and cancels nothing (NG-5).
+- A corrected visit meets the same rules as a new booking. A visit whose date has passed therefore cannot keep that date on correction. The PRD's Open Questions record whether that is intended.
+- The 2026-08-08 ADR's "a booked visit is immutable" no longer holds for date and description. Its NG-4 decision is unchanged.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the correction capability.
